WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.805
Eliot roamed through Mickey's Sports, browsing shelves stocked with tennis rackets and baseball bats.

2
00:00:09.806 --> 00:00:16.730
His younger brother, Sean, was searching for a new goalkeeper's jersey in the soccer aisle.

3
00:00:16.731 --> 00:00:23.397
Soccer tryouts started on Monday, and Sean wanted a new jersey for good luck.

4
00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:30.311
As Eliot headed back toward the soccer gear, he spotted an athletic boy looming over Sean.

5
00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:34.185
"Sean must have bumped into a friend," he thought.

6
00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:41.673
Then he saw the kid jab Sean with a finger. "Hey!" Eliot shouted.

7
00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:46.591
Sean's face turned bright red when he saw Eliot rushing toward him.

8
00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:53.904
"Stay off the soccer field, loser!" the kid snarled before he stalked off, snickering.

9
00:00:53.905 --> 00:00:57.039
"Who was that?" Eliot asked.

10
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.377
Sean held up a lime green jersey.

11
00:01:01.378 --> 00:01:04.443
"What do you think?" he joked weakly.

12
00:01:04.444 --> 00:01:08.099
"Does this go with my red hair and freckles?"

13
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.971
Before Eliot could reply, Sean shoved the jersey back in a pile on the shelf.

14
00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:22.259
"Let's get out of here. I can't afford a new jersey anyway."

15
00:01:22.268 --> 00:01:30.090
On Monday Eliot wasn't expecting to see Sean until dinnertime, after his first tryout session had ended.

16
00:01:30.091 --> 00:01:36.005
But when Eliot entered the kitchen after school, Sean was perched on a counter stool.

17
00:01:36.006 --> 00:01:39.202
"Sean! What are you doing here?"

18
00:01:39.203 --> 00:01:45.323
"I live here," he said sarcastically. "Remember?"

19
00:01:45.324 --> 00:01:48.885
"That's not what I meant," Eliot said.

20
00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:51.988
"Why aren't you at tryouts?"

21
00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:54.171
"Because I'm not trying out."

22
00:01:54.172 --> 00:01:56.002
"What?"

23
00:01:56.003 --> 00:02:00.730
"I won't make the team. So what's the point?"

24
00:02:00.731 --> 00:02:04.770
"The point is, you love soccer," Eliot said.

25
00:02:04.771 --> 00:02:09.783
"And you've been preparing for tryouts for months."

26
00:02:09.784 --> 00:02:14.665
"That was before I—" Sean's mouth abruptly snapped shut.

27
00:02:14.666 --> 00:02:17.680
"Before what?" Eliot demanded.

28
00:02:17.681 --> 00:02:23.018
Suddenly he flashed back to the scene at Mickey's Sports.

29
00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:25.991
"It's that kid from the store!

30
00:02:25.992 --> 00:02:29.187
He's the reason you skipped tryouts.

31
00:02:29.188 --> 00:02:33.947
You can't let him bully you into staying on the sidelines!"

32
00:02:33.948 --> 00:02:37.166
"It's my own fault," Sean said.

33
00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:41.450
"I shouldn't have bragged about my goalie skills to him."

34
00:02:41.451 --> 00:02:45.608
"Whoa." Eliot held up a hand.

35
00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:48.226
"It's not your fault.

36
00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:52.826
That kid is a bully, plain and simple."

37
00:02:52.827 --> 00:02:57.200
He frowned. "Has he harmed you physically?"

38
00:02:57.201 --> 00:02:59.406
Sean shook his head.

39
00:02:59.407 --> 00:03:02.216
"George just threatens to hurt me.

40
00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:06.262
Plus, he posts mean stuff about me on social media.

41
00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:11.398
I figured he'd finally leave me alone if I sat out tryouts this year."

42
00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:16.784
He sighed. "I can try out next year."

43
00:03:16.785 --> 00:03:20.192
"No way," Eliot said firmly.

44
00:03:20.193 --> 00:03:24.921
"You're not allowing some dumb bully to sabotage your soccer tryout."

45
00:03:24.922 --> 00:03:27.787
He glanced at the clock.

46
00:03:27.788 --> 00:03:30.578
"I'm driving you back to school.

47
00:03:30.579 --> 00:03:39.197
I'll give you some tips for dealing with bullies on the way."

48
00:03:39.198 --> 00:03:44.203
On Friday afternoon Eliot parked at the soccer field.

49
00:03:44.204 --> 00:03:47.985
"Today's the day," he thought anxiously.

50
00:03:47.986 --> 00:03:56.236
On the field the players huddled around Coach as she announced the names and positions of the players who'd made the team.

51
00:03:56.237 --> 00:04:00.606
Eliot didn't see George in the huddle.

52
00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:06.248
A few minutes later, Sean approached the car, head down.

53
00:04:06.249 --> 00:04:09.922
"Uh-oh," Eliot thought.

54
00:04:09.923 --> 00:04:12.976
Then Sean lifted his head—and grinned!

55
00:04:12.977 --> 00:04:20.185
Eliot hopped out of the car. "You made the team!"

56
00:04:20.186 --> 00:04:25.317
"Yep. I'm the starting goalie!" Sean said as Coach joined them.

57
00:04:25.318 --> 00:04:28.812
Coach shook Sean's hand.

58
00:04:28.813 --> 00:04:36.433
"Sean, you demonstrated great leadership on Monday by asking me to talk with everyone about bullying.

59
00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:41.610
It turns out you weren't the only one having issues with George."

60
00:04:41.611 --> 00:04:46.040
"Talking to an adult," Eliot thought with a smile.

61
00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:49.455
"That's a brilliant strategy for dealing with bullies.

62
00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:51.384
I wonder who thought of it."

63
00:04:51.385 --> 00:04:57.721
"Teamwork is important, and one bully can hurt the whole team," Coach went on.

64
00:04:57.722 --> 00:05:01.897
"I'm sorry I didn't know about the situation sooner.

65
00:05:01.898 --> 00:05:06.762
We now have a strict no-bullying policy, thanks to you."

66
00:05:06.763 --> 00:05:11.469
A few minutes later Eliot turned his car onto Main Street.

67
00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:14.639
"Where are we going?" Sean asked

68
00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.046
"Back to Mickey's Sports," he said.

69
00:05:18.047 --> 00:05:26.248
"To celebrate our victory, I'm going to buy you that green jersey!"

